    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI passes the `--ci` flag to the `frai-gate` subprocess. The issue occurred because:\n\n1. The `--ci` option is defined on the root `program` command (line 605)\n2. When running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js consumed the `--ci` flag at the root level before delegating to the `gate` subcommand\n3. The `args` array passed to the `gate` action handler only contained `['init']` without the `--ci` flag\n\n**The fix:** Changed the `gate` command's action handler to use `process.argv` directly instead of relying on the `args` parameter. This preserves all original command-line arguments including the `--ci` flag when passing them to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**Verification:** The fix has been tested and confirmed working:\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now successfully creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now successfully creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the missing piece)",
